# ── Claude Code working artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.claude-*/
**/CLAUDE.md
*.orig
*.rej

# ── build outputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bin/chirality-bin is COMMITTED on purpose: the source tree and the recompile
# harness ship with it, so a fresh checkout rebuilds and byte-compares rather
# than trusting it. Everything else a build writes is transient.
*.blob
*.elf
*.new
*.o
/blob
/build/
/C[0-9]
/D[0-9]

# `chirality compile FILE` with no -o writes an extensionless ELF beside its
# source. There is no glob for "filename without a dot" that would not also
# swallow a source file the day LAYOUT mints a sixth extension, and a source
# file silently untracked is worse than an artifact silently committed. So they
# are not ignored: pass `-o build/<name>`, or delete the artifact.

# ── Python, and only while tools/ still has any ──────────────────────────────
# Route step 1 replaces the 9 tools with chirality programs and deletes tools/.
# These three lines leave with it. Target: zero Python in the repo.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# ── editor / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.direnv/
.venv/
